# _headers = Security Headers Policy
#
# @summary
# Hardening headers applied to every response. The site has no backend,
# accounts, or third-party code: every script, style, font, and image is
# self-hosted, and the contact form is turned off and never submits, so the
# site sends nothing anywhere. That lets the Content-Security-Policy be
# strict rather than needing broad allowances.
#
# default-src 'self' is the fallback every unlisted directive inherits, so
# connect-src, font-src, img-src, and manifest-src need no lines of their own.
# The directives listed either need a different value than 'self' (frame-src,
# object-src), are never covered by default-src at all (base-uri,
# frame-ancestors, form-action), or just state the default for clarity
# (script-src, style-src). As in the sibling sites, style-src needs no
# 'unsafe-inline': the build ships no inline styles, and React sets its few
# dynamic styles (the menu rows' stagger indexes and the form tooltip's
# position) through the DOM, which the policy doesn't restrict. WebKit
# still reports one style-src-attr violation as React creates the contact
# form's select, from the browser's own styling of the control; checked
# 2026-10-12, the form draws identically with and without the policy, so
# it's harmless. The page's structured data script is a data block that
# never runs, so script-src doesn't need to allow it either.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security keeps browsers on HTTPS for two years across
# every subdomain, leaving out preload, which commits the domain to the
# browsers' built-in HTTPS list and is slow to undo. Referrer-Policy sends a
# referrer only to this same origin. Permissions-Policy turns off every
# powerful browser feature the site never uses.
#
# @author z4nta0 <https://github.com/z4nta0>

# What: Security Headers Rule. Why: Every response should refuse framing, sniffing, plain HTTP, unused browser features, and anything loaded from another origin. How: This applies the Content-Security-Policy, the permissions and referrer policies, HSTS, a nosniff content type, and a deny on framing to every path.
/*
	Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'
	Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
	Referrer-Policy: same-origin
	Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
	X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
	X-Frame-Options: DENY
